Add Rust-side "variable occurs at least twice" pass

Move the occurs-only-once check off the eqlog-eqlog side into a plain
Rust pass that walks each rule body, flags pairs of variable
occurrences that share a name in the scope graph, and reports any
remaining singletons as VariableOccursOnlyOnce. The Rust pass and
`check_eqlog` now both produce optional errors and are merged through
`CompileError`'s kind-precedence `Ord` so that, e.g., UndeclaredSymbol
still wins over a singleton variable in the same rule.
